        "original_id": "0836e3bc-61c5-510b-9133-200b2248112f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Plymouth City Airport, Newquay Cornwall Airport, Bristol Airport\n- People: Edward VIII, Prince of Wales\n- Companies: Air Southwest\n- Roles: King of the United Kingdom, Emperor of India\n\nFacts:\n- Plymouth City Airport opened on its site in 1925.\n- Plymouth City Airport was officially opened in 1931 by the future Edward VIII when he was Prince of Wales.\n- Edward VIII was born on 23 June 1894 and died on 28 May 1972.\n- Edward VIII was King of the United Kingdom and the Dominions of the British Empire, and Emperor of India, from 20 January 1936 until his abdication on 11 December 1936.\n- Air Southwest had its main base at Plymouth City Airport.\n- Air Southwest had hubs at Newquay Cornwall Airport and Bristol Airport.",
